schema: resource
object:
  title: "Smart wallets with passkey/guardian recovery (Base App, Argent \"Ready\")"
  type: resource
  resource_type: tool
  toolkit_route: layer-3-resource-graph
  related_concepts:
    - crypto-wallet-keys-not-money
  is_source_system_candidate: false
  link_status: unresolved
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-is-wallet.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: >-
    Newer wallet category described in the article: replaces the lone
    written recovery phrase with passkey sign-in (Face ID/fingerprint) plus
    recovery via phone backup or trusted "guardians" who can help restore
    access but cannot spend funds. Named examples: the Base App (Coinbase's
    wallet, replaced the older Coinbase Wallet in 2025) and Argent
    (rebranded "Ready" in mid-2025). Grouped as one resource entry since the
    article treats them as one emerging pattern rather than profiling each
    separately; no single canonical URL given for the pattern itself.
